(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA - MINISTRY OF SCIENCE & TECHNOLOGY - DEPARTMENT OF BIOTECHNOLOGY) Tj
T*
(OPERATIONAL GUIDELINES: BIOTECHNOLOGY IGNITION GRANT SCHEME \(BIRAC-BIG\) / BIOTECHNOLOGY INDUSTRY RESEARCH ASSISTANCE COUNCIL \(BIRAC\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Overview & Objective:) Tj
T*
(Flagship early-stage grant-in-aid of up to Rs. 50 Lakh for biotech, medtech,) Tj
T*
(diagnostics, agri-biotech, and industrial biotechnology innovations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Eligibility Criteria:) Tj
T*
(1. Biotech startup incorporated for not more than 5 years, or an individual) Tj
T*
(   innovator with verified institutional backing.) Tj
T*
(2. Majority shareholding \(> 51%\) held by Indian citizens who are) Tj
T*
(   researchers, scientists, or medical entrepreneurs.) Tj
T*
(3. Startups must possess an incubator affiliation or independent laboratory) Tj
T*
(   access.) Tj
T*
(4. Clear scientific hypothesis and novel intellectual property path.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Financial Assistance and Subsidy:) Tj
T*
(1. Grant-in-aid up to Rs. 50 Lakh for milestone-based research and proof-of-) Tj
T*
(   concept validation over 18 months, with zero equity dilution.) Tj
T*
(3. Maximum financial assistance cap is Rs 50.0 Lakh per unit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Mandatory Documents Checklist:) Tj
T*
(1. Company Incorporation Certificate / GST) Tj
T*
(2. Detailed Scientific Research Proposal with experimental milestones) Tj
T*
(3. IP disclosure / patent search report) Tj
T*
(4. Laboratory affiliation / Letter of Support from BIRAC-partner incubator) Tj
T*
(5. Promoter CVs and publication records) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Application Procedure:) Tj
T*
(1. Mode: Online via BIRAC Portal \(Biannual calls in January and July\)) Tj
T*
(2. Official Portal: https://birac.nic.in/desc_new.php?id=37) Tj
T*
